            <ArticleTitle>[Synchronous sigmoideum- and caecum volvulus].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>V04150346</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">V04150346</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This case presents a synchronous sigmoid- and caecum volvulus in a 69-year old man with Parkinson's disease, hypertension and previous history of colonic volvulus. On admission the patient had abdominal pain, nausea, vomiting and constipation. The CT scan showed a sigmoid volvulus with a dilated caecum. The synchronous sigmoideum- and caecum volvulus was diagnosed intraoperatively. Total colectomy and ileostomy was performed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
